199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (During the implementation, I initially tried to use more advanced deep learning models such as EfficientNet and segmentation models like U-Net to improve accuracy and lesion detection. However, due to the lack of GPU support and limited computational resources, training these heavy models on CPU was very slow and impractical. Additionally, the dataset size was relatively small and imbalanced, which led to overfitting when using deeper architectures. Because of these limitations, I shifted to a lightweight pretrained ResNet18 model using transfer learning, which provided stable performance and faster training. This allowed me to successfully implement the detection system and further extend it by adding PASI scoring for severity estimation.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
